  "id": "magical-thinking",
  "term": "magical thinking",
  "definition": "Magical thinking is a pattern of believing that one’s thoughts or acts can bring about outcomes in ways that are not realistically possible. It can appear in everyday life as well as in mental health problems, including obsessive-compulsive disorder and schizophrenia-related thinking, and may sometimes be linked with distress or impaired functioning.",
